  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 122 PM CDT Wed Aug 26 2026\n\nModels slowly bring a weak cold front into our region this \nevening and overnight, generating a smattering of convection \nmainly late this afternoon and evening. The model blend \nproduces chances in the 15-35% range, with the higher chances \nmore focused across our eastern half of counties this evening. \nMany areas will remain dry, but locations that see thunderstorms\nmay see brief heavy rainfall. \n\nBehind the front, drier air will be slow to arrive, finally\nfiltering into our region by Thursday night. Temperatures will\nremain fairly seasonable Thursday through Saturday, but the \nlower humidity will make it feel a little more comfortable. \nWinds will shift to the south Saturday into Saturday night, \nresulting in a warming trend Sunday into next week. High \ntemperatures will be in the lower to middle 90s Sunday, and the \nmiddle to upper 90s by Tuesday and Wednesday. Dew points through\nthis period will max out around 70 degrees, keeping the heat \nfrom being too oppressive this time around.",
